    "hypothesis": "When the average pairwise correlation of the nine sector ETFs is unusually high (its trailing 252-day z-score over a 21-day window), the VIX falls more over the next 10 trading days than its own 5-day momentum and log level predict. Formally: in the regression of the forward 10-day log VIX change on the correlation z-score, 5-day VIX momentum, and log VIX, the coefficient on the z-score is negative.\n",
    "primary": {
      "window": 21,
      "horizon": 10,
      "include_controls": true,
      "alpha": 0.05
    },
    "note": "Formed after the original study found a negative z coefficient on 2007-2026 data, and after an exploration run confirmed the same sign for sector ETFs on 2007-2026. Fixed before any 1998-12-22 to 2007-04-30 data was analyzed. Test: one-sided Newey-West (HAC, maxlags = horizon) t-test on the z coefficient over eligible holdout days. Only the holdout result is confirmatory; the window and horizon match the original preregistered spec rather than the best exploration result.\n"
  },
